-- title:
--   Genus bound for dim_ℂ S₂(Γ(N))
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number with $2 \le N$, let $\Gamma(N) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ be the principal congruence subgroup of level $N$, and let $\mu_N$ denote the index in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma(N)$ together with $-I$ (formally, the index of the join of $\Gamma(N)$ and the subgroup of integer powers of $-I$). Write $S_2(\Gamma(N))$ for the complex vector space of weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma(N)$ and $\dim_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma(N))$ for its rank as a $\mathbb C$-module. The assertion is the inequality of natural numbers
--   $$12N + N\mu_N \;\le\; 12N \cdot \dim_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma(N)) + 6\mu_N .$$
--   All arithmetic takes place in $\mathbb N$, so the statement is a cleared-denominator form of the lower bound $\dim_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma(N)) \ge 1 + \mu_N(N-6)/(12N)$, the right-hand side being the genus of $X(N)$. Only this one inequality is asserted: no upper bound on $\dim_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma(N))$, and no identification of the dimension with the genus, is part of the conclusion.
--
--   This is the existence (lower bound) half of the classical identity $\dim_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma(N)) = g(X(N))$, in the cleared-denominator shape in which the genus of $X(N)$ is computed from the index $\mu_N$. It is used in [`ModularCurve.finrank_parabolicHoms_Gamma_le_two_mul_finrank_cuspForm`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_parabolicHoms_Gamma_le_two_mul_finrank_cuspForm), and thence in the Eichler–Shimura comparison between parabolic cohomology of congruence subgroups and weight-$2$ cusp forms.
-- source:
